  "lectures": [
    {
      "id": "31404648",
      "title": "Expo Alternatives",
      "lectureOrder": 224,
      "videoOrder": 218,
      "sourceHash": "ffd26234dd7188a02c5d635874b499f78b65d5964bdc0ad11f7750308125cd46",
      "cues": [
        {
          "id": 1,
          "start": 2.251,
          "end": 4.73,
          "en": "[Maximilian Schwarzmüller] Now Expo is really useful",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 2,
          "start": 4.73,
          "end": 6.79,
          "en": "because it helps us during development",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 3,
          "start": 6.79,
          "end": 10.71,
          "en": "and it makes development so easy and frictionless.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 4,
          "start": 10.71,
          "end": 12.91,
          "en": "What we used in this course is called",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 5,
          "start": 12.91,
          "end": 15.61,
          "en": "the Expo Managed Workflow.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 6,
          "start": 15.61,
          "end": 17.06,
          "en": "That's what we used in this course.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 7,
          "start": 17.06,
          "end": 19.86,
          "en": "And that means that we used the Expo Go App",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 8,
          "start": 19.86,
          "end": 22.48,
          "en": "and a project created with Expo",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 9,
          "start": 22.48,
          "end": 26.46,
          "en": "with the Expo init command where during creation,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 10,
          "start": 26.46,
          "end": 29.56,
          "en": "we chose the Managed Workflow template,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 11,
          "start": 29.56,
          "end": 33.13,
          "en": "if you recall that. And the advantage of this is",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 12,
          "start": 33.13,
          "end": 35.61,
          "en": "that we don't just have the Expo Go App",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 13,
          "start": 35.61,
          "end": 39.13,
          "en": "but we also have a project with a lot of configuration",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 14,
          "start": 39.13,
          "end": 42.11,
          "en": "taken away from us in the positive way",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 15,
          "start": 42.11,
          "end": 44.51,
          "en": "so that we don't have to worry about that.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 16,
          "start": 44.51,
          "end": 48.15,
          "en": "We also get an app that already has a lot of things built in",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 17,
          "start": 48.15,
          "end": 50.97,
          "en": "which made working with certain features,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 18,
          "start": 50.97,
          "end": 54.15,
          "en": "for example, native device features much easier",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 19,
          "start": 54.15,
          "end": 55.61,
          "en": "because we don't have to worry",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 20,
          "start": 55.61,
          "end": 59.11,
          "en": "about configuring any third party packages",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 21,
          "start": 59.11,
          "end": 61.293,
          "en": "when we wanted to use them and so on.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 22,
          "start": 62.2,
          "end": 66.61,
          "en": "Sometimes though, you want less configuration out of the box",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 23,
          "start": 66.61,
          "end": 70.3,
          "en": "and you want more control. And for those cases,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 24,
          "start": 70.3,
          "end": 74.55,
          "en": "you could consider using the Expo Bare Workflow.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 25,
          "start": 74.55,
          "end": 77.01,
          "en": "And we're going to take a look at how that works",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 26,
          "start": 77.01,
          "end": 78.75,
          "en": "and what the difference is later",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 27,
          "start": 78.75,
          "end": 80.503,
          "en": "in this course section here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 28,
          "start": 81.41,
          "end": 84.11,
          "en": "Alternatively, you could also build projects",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 29,
          "start": 84.11,
          "end": 86.72,
          "en": "that don't use Expo in any way,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 30,
          "start": 86.72,
          "end": 90.26,
          "en": "so that you don't use this company and package in any way.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 31,
          "start": 90.26,
          "end": 93.38,
          "en": "And you could just create and manage projects",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 32,
          "start": 93.38,
          "end": 96.46000000000001,
          "en": "with just the React Native CLI,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 33,
          "start": 96.46000000000001,
          "end": 98.86,
          "en": "which is a command line interface provided",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 34,
          "start": 98.86,
          "end": 100.87299999999999,
          "en": "by the React Native team itself.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 35,
          "start": 101.74000000000001,
          "end": 104.74000000000001,
          "en": "Now let's take a quick look at all these differences.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 36,
          "start": 104.74000000000001,
          "end": 107.49000000000001,
          "en": "Of course we're always going to see them in action",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 37,
          "start": 107.49000000000001,
          "end": 108.743,
          "en": "throughout this section.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 38,
          "start": 110.21000000000001,
          "end": 113.00999999999999,
          "en": "For the Managed Workflow, as we saw in this course,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 39,
          "start": 113.00999999999999,
          "end": 115.78999999999999,
          "en": "an advantage is that it's easy to set up and work with,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 40,
          "start": 115.78999999999999,
          "end": 118.56,
          "en": "we have quick and frictionless development.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 41,
          "start": 118.56,
          "end": 120.8,
          "en": "We don't really have to worry that much",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 42,
          "start": 120.8,
          "end": 122.78,
          "en": "about configuring things,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 43,
          "start": 122.78,
          "end": 125.68,
          "en": "especially if we add third party packages",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 44,
          "start": 125.68,
          "end": 129.74,
          "en": "that use native device features like user's location",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 45,
          "start": 129.74,
          "end": 133.27,
          "en": "that is super easy, we didn't have to do a lot there.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 46,
          "start": 133.27,
          "end": 135.48,
          "en": "And we can, as you will see",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 47,
          "start": 135.48,
          "end": 137.05,
          "en": "in the next course section,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 48,
          "start": 137.05,
          "end": 139.99,
          "en": "build cross platform standalone apps.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 49,
          "start": 139.99,
          "end": 142.623,
          "en": "So we have no restriction regarding that.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 50,
          "start": 144,
          "end": 145.87,
          "en": "Now, if we need more control,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 51,
          "start": 145.87,
          "end": 150.87,
          "en": "if we for sample need to write our own native code in Swift",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 52,
          "start": 151.17000000000002,
          "end": 154.2,
          "en": "or Objective-C or Android or Kotlin",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 53,
          "start": 154.2,
          "end": 157.46,
          "en": "and we need to mix that with our React Native code",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 54,
          "start": 157.46,
          "end": 159.723,
          "en": "which is possible in React Native apps,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 55,
          "start": 159.723,
          "end": 163.8,
          "en": "then we might consider switching to the Bare workflow.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 56,
          "start": 163.8,
          "end": 166.84,
          "en": "This is still a React Native project created",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 57,
          "start": 166.84,
          "end": 170.99,
          "en": "with the help of Expo using some Expo features",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 58,
          "start": 170.99,
          "end": 173.75,
          "en": "but less of those Expo features.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 59,
          "start": 173.75,
          "end": 177.15,
          "en": "It's still relatively easy to set up and work with.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 60,
          "start": 177.15,
          "end": 180.82,
          "en": "And we still have a convenient development experience",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 61,
          "start": 180.82,
          "end": 185.52,
          "en": "though we often won't use the Expo Go app, for example,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 62,
          "start": 185.52,
          "end": 187.16,
          "en": "because that app does not work",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 63,
          "start": 187.16,
          "end": 189.7,
          "en": "if you add your own custom native code",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 64,
          "start": 189.7,
          "end": 192.033,
          "en": "that should be mixed with your Ava code.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 65,
          "start": 193.34,
          "end": 196.25,
          "en": "In addition, you might need to worry",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 66,
          "start": 196.25,
          "end": 198.53,
          "en": "a bit more about configuring things.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 67,
          "start": 198.53,
          "end": 202.13,
          "en": "This can also be an advantage that you can configure more",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 68,
          "start": 202.13,
          "end": 205.66,
          "en": "with this approach, but you also have to configure more.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 69,
          "start": 205.66,
          "end": 209.68,
          "en": "And that can be an advantage, but also a huge disadvantage.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 70,
          "start": 209.68,
          "end": 212.41,
          "en": "And we're going to see what I mean regarding that",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 71,
          "start": 212.41,
          "end": 214.94,
          "en": "throughout this course section.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 72,
          "start": 214.94,
          "end": 217.43,
          "en": "Now regarding the apps you produce,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 73,
          "start": 217.43,
          "end": 221.34,
          "en": "you still produce cross platform standalone apps.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 74,
          "start": 221.34,
          "end": 224.1,
          "en": "You can still use this built service provided",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 75,
          "start": 224.1,
          "end": 226.99,
          "en": "by the Expo company at which we'll take a look",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 76,
          "start": 226.99,
          "end": 228.5,
          "en": "in the next course section.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 77,
          "start": 228.5,
          "end": 230.75,
          "en": "And you can still build your apps",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 78,
          "start": 230.75,
          "end": 232.44,
          "en": "in a pretty convenient way.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 79,
          "start": 232.44,
          "end": 235.89,
          "en": "This does not change, but you have more control",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 80,
          "start": 235.89,
          "end": 238.563,
          "en": "but also more things you have to do.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 81,
          "start": 239.86,
          "end": 242.13,
          "en": "Now you can also build React Native apps",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 82,
          "start": 242.13,
          "end": 243.87,
          "en": "without Expo at all though.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 83,
          "start": 243.87,
          "end": 246.28,
          "en": "When you use just the React Native CLI,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 84,
          "start": 246.28,
          "end": 249.27,
          "en": "you have a more complex setup that's required.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 85,
          "start": 249.27,
          "end": 252.9,
          "en": "You have to do more things on your own all the time,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 86,
          "start": 252.9,
          "end": 254.5,
          "en": "but once everything is set up,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 87,
          "start": 254.5,
          "end": 257.04,
          "en": "development is still pretty convenient.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 88,
          "start": 257.04,
          "end": 261.55,
          "en": "But when you add third party packages, when you need to tap",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 89,
          "start": 261.55,
          "end": 263.69,
          "en": "into native device features,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 90,
          "start": 263.69,
          "end": 267.19,
          "en": "that often requires more configuration effort",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 91,
          "start": 267.19,
          "end": 269.57,
          "en": "and can be more cumbersome.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 92,
          "start": 269.57,
          "end": 271.71,
          "en": "Of course, again, the advantage could be",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 93,
          "start": 271.71,
          "end": 275.15999999999997,
          "en": "that you have more control, but you should be aware of that.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 94,
          "start": 275.15999999999997,
          "end": 278.32,
          "en": "Another potential disadvantage is,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 95,
          "start": 278.32,
          "end": 281.62,
          "en": "that when you're using the React Native CLI,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 96,
          "start": 281.62,
          "end": 285.3,
          "en": "you can of course look for certain third party companies",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 97,
          "start": 285.3,
          "end": 289.14,
          "en": "and providers that might still offer you cloud builds",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 98,
          "start": 289.14,
          "end": 291.47,
          "en": "of your apps so that you can still build",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 99,
          "start": 291.47,
          "end": 293.21,
          "en": "for multiple platforms.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 100,
          "start": 293.21,
          "end": 295.53,
          "en": "But unlike with Expo, this feature,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 101,
          "start": 295.53,
          "end": 298.17,
          "en": "this support is not built into your app.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 102,
          "start": 298.17,
          "end": 301.62,
          "en": "There is no easy way of getting this set up",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 103,
          "start": 301.62,
          "end": 305.35,
          "en": "and therefore, indeed, you have to build your apps locally,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 104,
          "start": 305.35,
          "end": 308.25,
          "en": "which means that for example, on Windows machines,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 105,
          "start": 308.25,
          "end": 310.64,
          "en": "you can't build iOS apps",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 106,
          "start": 310.64,
          "end": 313.46,
          "en": "because that is a restriction enforced by Apple.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 107,
          "start": 313.46,
          "end": 315.34,
          "en": "You can't do that.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 108,
          "start": 315.34,
          "end": 318.16,
          "en": "So these are the different approaches we have.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 109,
          "start": 318.16,
          "end": 321.15,
          "en": "We used the Managed Workflow extensively",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 110,
          "start": 321.15,
          "end": 322.53,
          "en": "throughout this course.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 111,
          "start": 322.53,
          "end": 323.84,
          "en": "In the next lectures,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 112,
          "start": 323.84,
          "end": 327.02,
          "en": "we're going to see how we could use the Bare Workflow",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 113,
          "start": 327.02,
          "end": 329.78,
          "en": "instead before we then also take a look",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 114,
          "start": 329.78,
          "end": 331.557,
          "en": "at using the React Native CLI.",
          "zh": ""
        }
      ]
    }
